 {"status": "pending", "id": "AUG-196", "title": "Shrink guard is pre-commit only: a --no-verify local commit lands the shrink and is caught post-landing by CI --recent (how 45a29b9 landed)", "detail": {"fingerprint": "78085685212be712b9e55b1b11dcf01070b6dfefa8c28b5c1d58f830da9d5b78"}, "priority": "P3", "source": null, "reasoning": "Judge run ecef6bee (AUG-194 re-judge at f10ca29) uncovered failure mode 1: hooks are client-side; --no-verify bypasses the pre-commit shrink check, and the CI '--recent' step only catches it after landing. 45a29b9 landed exactly this way. Options: a pre-push hook managed block, or a fleet-strand-push/net-level check before push.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-21T17:59:55+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-21T17:59:55+00:00", "foreman_note": null, "capability_tags": [], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null, "sessions": null, "type": null, "acceptance_criteria": "AC1: a second enforcement point exists beyond the pre-commit hook (pre-push managed block or push-path check) that refuses to push a board shrink. AC2: proven on a scratch clone: commit a shrink with --no-verify, attempt push path, expect refusal naming counts+lost ids. AC3: BOARD_ALLOW_SHRINK=1 override still works and stays loud.", "worker_summary": null}
 {"status": "pending", "id": "AUG-SURGERY-1", "title": "Non-JEV support for the ask loop + proper caching", "detail": {"metadata": {}, "fingerprint": "b45a3c225c94865b8519eff47507b5e93b8b985dc2051ce49b12dc9bf4735ee7"}, "priority": "P2", "source": null, "reasoning": null, "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-21T21:07:34+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-21T21:07:34+00:00", "foreman_note": null, "capability_tags": [], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null, "sessions": null, "type": "feat", "acceptance_criteria": "1) Pluggable question-generator behind config: JEV stays default; non-JEV path selectable when JEV unavailable/budget-thin (deterministic heuristic candidates from low-confidence decisions + coverage gaps, and/or an LLM on any configured provider e.g. synthetic/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017). 2) Candidate cache keyed by (namespace, project, corpus state hash): repeated ask calls in one session do not re-pay embedding round-trips or re-generate the same batch; cache invalidates on corpus/decision changes. 3) Recall-result cache keyed by (query, corpus version) with TTL: the ~20s embedding provider round-trip is paid once per distinct query. 4) Tests: full ask->answer round completes with JEV disabled end-to-end; cache hit proven by zero second-call provider round-trip; invalidation proven after a decision write. Context: the CHD surgery loop (owner directive 2026-11-21) currently hard-depends on JEV via task-router; owner: 'include non jev support for the loop with proper caching etc'.", "worker_summary": null}
 {"status": "pending", "id": "AUG-SURGERY-2", "title": "Surgery loop hardening: paraphrase dedup, domain-binding propagation, scope param, embedding degradation", "detail": {"metadata": {}, "fingerprint": "9871a9ffe662ec35eb0b84bc612aae1deefe7257a13eb25e3df4ffa3493e1769"}, "priority": "P2", "source": null, "reasoning": null, "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-21T21:09:57+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-21T21:09:57+00:00", "foreman_note": null, "capability_tags": [], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null, "sessions": null, "type": "bug", "acceptance_criteria": "1) Paraphrase dedup: 8 ask rounds re-surfaced the same 3 topics as new Q-ids (Q-000016/023 restate Q-000005; Q-000018/020/024/028 restate Q-000009; Q-000025/026 restate Q-000007) - the JEV already_answered gate must drop semantic paraphrases, not just exact matches. 2) Domain binding must propagate to answers: ask records questions with domain='' and answer does not inherit it, so 20 of 33 decisions landed in the (none) bucket and the coverage map only moved when --domain was passed manually; answer should default its domain from the question row or the parent decision. 3) answer --scope design is rejected ('unknown decision scope: expected project, bundle') - either accept a design scope or document why project-only. 4) Intermittent 'embedding.healthy=false' on some answer writes (D-050, D-059, D-060 keyword-searchable only) while recall reported healthy on the same session - investigate the write-path embedding probe and make the degraded-write state loud, not silent. Evidence: .tmp-surgery-log.txt + .tmp-surgery-summary.md (surgery run 2026-11-21, 33 decisions, mean conf 0.69->0.78).", "worker_summary": null}
+{"status": "pending", "id": "AUG-197", "title": "The Tier-1 gate cannot complete on a loaded box: tests(full) timed out at 3000s (32%) and the live DuckBrain arm 409s on foreign namespace sync locks, so any commit touching the suite is blocked", "detail": {"metadata": {}, "fingerprint": "5b4b0ffedbf0ef69b3c39f6a50ad1c9e95119bcc96cbf0ed24b53b4ca3749cc4"}, "priority": "P2", "source": null, "reasoning": "Measured on tick auger-foreman-2026-11-22-04-52-38: the worker's gitreins guard ran tests(full) for 3000s, reached 32%, then was killed (AUG-081 process-group timeout) and reported 'first_failing_test: none detected'. A separate -x run failed first on tests/test_auger.py::test_init_declares_every_table_the_module_defines with 'ERROR at teardown ... DELETE returned 409: Push in flight for auger-pytest-... (native sync lock held by pid 2835668)'; that same test passes alone at the base commit, so the failure is contention from concurrent live runs, not a code regression. Result: a board-only or small-diff commit cannot land through the guarded path while the box is loaded.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-22T06:26:00+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-22T06:26:00+00:00", "foreman_note": null, "capability_tags": ["gate", "ci", "tests", "duckbrain"], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null, "sessions": null, "type": "bug", "acceptance_criteria": "AC1: the gate's pytest arm finishes or reports a bounded, attributable result under load >=25 on 16 cores (shard, per-file selection, or a documented cap that fails closed on timeout with the first-failing test named, not 'first_failing_test: none detected'). AC2: a live DuckBrain namespace teardown that hits 409 'Push in flight' held by a FOREIGN pid is classified as environment contention (SKIP/ERROR attributed) instead of failing the suite, and the test-side namespace is reaped on the next